Subject: gcc/config/i386/substrate.h: psABI DWARF register numbers

The i386 target took i386.h's default DEBUGGER_REGNO, the old DBX map, in
which %ebp is DWARF register 4 and %esp is 5 -- the reverse of the i386
psABI numbering that every other ELF i386 target selects (gnu-user.h,
sysv4.h, i386elf.h) and that gdb, readelf and libunwind assume.  CFI was
self-consistent, since libgcc's unwinder is compiled with the same map, so
C++ exceptions worked; but gdb computed every CFA from the wrong register
and showed one-frame backtraces with zeroed arguments.

Select svr4_debugger_register_map.  This changes the register numbers in
.eh_frame and .debug_frame, so libgcc and everything carrying unwind
tables has to be rebuilt together.  x86_64 already used the psABI map.
---
diff --git a/gcc/config/i386/substrate.h b/gcc/config/i386/substrate.h
--- a/gcc/config/i386/substrate.h
+++ b/gcc/config/i386/substrate.h
@@ -59,4 +59,14 @@
 #undef  TARGET_ASM_FILE_END
 #define TARGET_ASM_FILE_END file_end_indicate_exec_stack
 
+/* DWARF register numbers: the i386 psABI's (System V ABI, Intel386
+   supplement, figure 3-36), in which %esp is 4 and %ebp is 5, as on every
+   other ELF i386 target.  Without this the port inherits i386.h's default
+   map, the old DBX one, which has the two the other way round: everything
+   built agreed with itself (libgcc's unwinder uses the same map), but a
+   debugger computed each frame from the wrong register.  */
+#undef  DEBUGGER_REGNO
+#define DEBUGGER_REGNO(n) \
+  (TARGET_64BIT ? debugger64_register_map[n] : svr4_debugger_register_map[n])
+
 #endif /* GCC_I386_SUBSTRATE_H */
